Subject: [#94-3-21] Water Fuel Cells

Geoff Burch writes:
>        I have a question pertaining to Water Fuel Cell technology.  I
>recently met a man named Stan Meyer who was a customer in a cafe where I
>work, who claims to have designed a way to convert all heat-engines to
>engines that run off of the covalent bonds between hydrogen and oxygen,
>thus creating a non-pollutive, efficient machine that the fuel will never
>run out for.  Steve, upon request furnished an inch-thick brochure
>containing the information based upon how it works.
>
>        Has anyone heard of this?  What info can someone please send me
>concerning this?  What is the validity and possibility of it's fruition?
>

This is a  scam but sounds like it is based loosely on real fuel cells.
They start with hydrogen and oxygen, make water and release energy in the
process. Fuel cells convert the energy directly from chemical bonds to
electricity. Combustion engines can convert hydrogen to mechanical power
much as a fossil fuel engine does. 

I wonder what the scam artist wrote in all those pages.



