One of the ideas I've had for an interesting project would
be to set up a service that acts as a buffer for waste
material, before it actually goes to the landfill. The idea
is to take interesting "waste", such as scrap metals,
old furniture, etc. and act as a short-term storage
facility for these thing. This could be done more efficiently
by taking requests from different parties on what they
need, and then use that as the basis of what is taken
in. By acting as an intermediary, instead of dumping waste
into the trash, a business could say sell it the
service for a small amount (making money on what it would
normally throw away at no profit), and the service
would find buyer's for it... Actually this is a service
I'd like to have for my own uses, and a similar project
was a design problem for an undergrad compsci course
I was in....

